----- stdout -----
Generate shell completion scripts.

Writes the selected completion script to stdout so it can be redirected, sourced, or installed by a package manager without temporary files.

Usage: pina completions <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Shell whose completion script should be generated
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/pina
  pina completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_pina
  pina completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/pina.fish

----- stderr -----
